# Worker memory report, 04:15 UTC = 09:45 IST on weekdays - about 30 minutes
# after the 09:14 NSE open, so the window it summarises is real market-hours
# load rather than the near-idle out-of-hours captures.
#
# Exists because the interesting number only appears under load: the worker
# allocates a large TRANSIENT native burst inside captureOnce() (~964MB
# measured out-of-hours, ~2.5GB during the session) which is invisible to
# process.memoryUsage()'s heap figures. See CLAUDE.md's worker-memory entry.
#
# Writes one dated file per day; read the newest with
#   ssh dhan-ec2 'cat /opt/option-decode-native/logs/memory-reports/$(date +%F).txt'
# Not rotated by ops/logrotate/option-decode (that covers *.log only) - these
# are small, one per weekday.
15 4 * * 1-5 root mkdir -p /opt/option-decode-native/logs/memory-reports && /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/worker-memory-report.sh >> /opt/option-decode-native/logs/memory-reports/$(date +\%F).txt 2>&1

# Five minutes later, decide whether that report is worth an email. Separate
# line rather than chained onto the one above so a mail failure can never mark
# the report job itself as failed, and so the report is already written and
# closed before anything reads it.
#
# Regression-only, plus a Friday summary. A daily "all fine" email gets
# filtered within a fortnight and takes the important one with it.
20 4 * * 1-5 root /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/worker-memory-alert.sh >> /opt/option-decode-native/logs/memory-reports/alert.log 2>&1

# The API had no memory instrumentation at all until 2026-08-31, so when its
# cgroup memory rose over the Live Order work there was nothing to say why.
# Same two-step shape as the worker's above: write the report, then decide
# separately whether it is worth an email, so a mail failure can never mark the
# report job failed.
25 4 * * 1-5 root mkdir -p /opt/option-decode-native/logs/memory-reports && /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/api-memory-report.sh >> /opt/option-decode-native/logs/memory-reports/api-$(date +\%F).txt 2>&1
30 4 * * 1-5 root /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/api-memory-alert.sh >> /opt/option-decode-native/logs/memory-reports/alert.log 2>&1
